# Line-ending normalization, stated in the repo rather than in each machine's config.
#
# Without this file the result depends on the cloner's `core.autocrlf`: a collaborator with
# autocrlf=false sees CRLF where another sees LF, and any file Power BI Desktop touches comes back
# with its whole diff changed even when not a line was edited.
#
# The eol=lf form matters: a bare `* text=auto` or any `eol=crlf` rule makes some tooling reject
# the repo on a line-ending rule. So there are no eol=crlf rules here; the working copy is
# normalized to LF on add, and the diff does not grow.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run inside Linux CI. With CRLF the shebang becomes "#!/bin/sh\r" and the script
# is no longer found.
*.sh        text eol=lf

# Binary blobs: never normalize.
*.pbix      binary
*.abf       binary
*.parquet   binary
